# The corpus binary is never committed — see CLAUDE.md invariant 4.
# corpus/manifest.json pins it; the tool fetches and hash-verifies on first use.
corpus/*.sqlite
corpus/*.sqlite-*
corpus/*.zip
corpus/cache/

# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# macOS
.DS_Store

# superpowers execution scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Harness-created worktrees live here. Not ignored until 2026-10-24, when a
# `git status` on `main` during a worktree session listed the whole tree as
# untracked -- one `git add -A` from committing a copy of the repo into itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# No mapping table lives anywhere but `data/decisions.tsv` (D63). This exists
# because the validation maneuver `review/README.md` describes -- copy the
# reviewed Humble table into `data/` and run the real gates -- leaves an
# untracked, licence-gated 205 KB file behind if it is interrupted, and the
# repository is going public for Homebrew. The guards that refuse such a file
# are `the_decisions_file_is_the_one_that_ships` and `cargo xtask
# check-mappings`; this is the belt to their braces.
data/mappings/
data/**/*.tsv
!data/decisions.tsv
